            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.495,
            0.846,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can a similar classification be done based on equality of angles? Is there any relation between these two classifications? We will answer these questions in a later chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.551,
            0.845,
            0.59
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We used angle measures when classifying a triangle as a rightangled triangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.597,
            0.782,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? What are the other types of triangles based on angle measures?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.628,
            0.847,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A classification of triangles based on their angle measures is acuteangled, right-angled and obtuse-angled triangles. We have already seen what a right-angled triangle is. It is a triangle with one right angle. Similarly, an obtuse-angled triangle has one obtuse angle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.712,
            0.752,
            0.752
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What could an acute-angled triangle be? Can we define it as a triangle with one acute angle? Why not?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.818,
            0.702,
            0.905,
            0.755
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 17,
              "bbox": [
                0.818,
                0.702,
                0.905,
                0.755
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_24_image_17.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.762,
            0.763,
            0.782
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In an "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "acute-angled",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " triangle, all three angles are acute angles."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.789,
            0.293,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.816,
            0.845,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Construct a triangle ABC with BC = 5 cm, AB = 6 cm, CA = 5 cm. Construct an altitude from A to BC."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.858,
            0.845,
            0.896
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Construct a triangle TRY with RY = 4 cm, TR = 7 cm, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{R} = 140^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Construct an altitude from T to RY."
            }
          ]
        },
